    <string name="hands_dealt_intro"><![CDATA[Choose how the strategy trainer deals its hands.<br><br><b>%1$s</b> deals hands as often as a shuffled shoe would to a player following the strategy chart, hands of 3 or more cards and doubled hands included.<br><br><b>%2$s</b> deals a hand, your two cards against the dealer\'s upcard, more often the worse you do with it: get it right half as often and it comes up twice as often. Hands of 3 or more cards, and doubled hands, count by their total. Where a card count, or the suits of a bonus hand, change the move, each move is a hand of its own. A hand you haven\'t answered yet counts as 50%% right.<br><br>Either way, <b>%3$s</b> and <b>%4$s</b>, switched on below, deal more of the hands where a card count or a bonus can change the move.]]></string>
    <string name="hand_types_intro"><![CDATA[Choose which types of hand the strategy trainer deals, by their correct move under the current table rules. If none of the types switched on can come up under these rules, the trainer deals every type.<br><br><b>%1$s</b> deals at least 1 hand in 4 from hands of 3 or more cards where the number of cards changes the move, as in D5 or S6 on the strategy chart, so even the rare 5- and 6-card ones come up often.<br><br><b>%2$s</b> deals at least 1 hand in 10 from two-card hands that could make a 6-7-8 or 7-7-7 bonus on a square with a bonus mark, as in S4* or P$ on the strategy chart, in the suits that make it and, beside them, the same cards in other suits.<br><br>The <b>Already doubled</b> types deal a hand just doubled where the strategy chart says double, its double card sideways. Stand on it, redouble where the table rules allow it, or rescue it: take back the double and give up the original bet.]]></string>
